WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.540
Signed momentum lets you predict the

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:03.060
motion after a collision.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.850
These two carts will stick together.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.810
Cart A has a mass of two kilograms

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:08.430
and moves right at three metres per

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.250
second.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.110
Cart B has a mass of one kilogram

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.590
and moves left at one metre per

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.440
second.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.990
Choose right as positive.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.120
Our system includes both carts, and

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.930
the net external horizontal force is

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.460
zero during the collision.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.570
Predict the direction before

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.680
calculating.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.180
Choose right, left, or at rest, and

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.420
write one reason.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.710
Pause the video now.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.330
Compare momentum contributions

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.310
rather than simply comparing speeds.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.970
Momentum is mass multiplied by

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:33.930
velocity.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.950
In this one-dimensional calculation,

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.940
a positive momentum points right and

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.840
a negative momentum points left.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.320
Mass stays positive.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.730
It is the velocity's sign that

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.030
carries the direction.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.320
The initial momentum has two

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.500
contributions.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.820
Cart A contributes plus six, while

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.710
cart B contributes minus one, in

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.420
kilogram metres per second.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.210
Their total is plus five, so the

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.990
combined motion will be right.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.620
If you obtained seven, you added

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.020
magnitudes and lost the leftward

00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.910
direction.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.540
The shared final velocity belongs to

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.610
both carts.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.730
Which mass must multiply it: three

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.910
kilograms, two kilograms, or one

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:07.750
kilogram?

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.830
Pause and decide before continuing.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.390
Conservation of momentum connects

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.850
before and after for the whole

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.090
two-cart system.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.310
The combined mass is three

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.320
kilograms, because both carts move

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.010
with the same final velocity.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.230
Each cart can change its own

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.740
momentum while the total stays

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.630
constant.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.460
Solving for velocity gives five

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.690
divided by three.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.870
Keep that full value during working.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.270
The positive sign agrees with our

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.170
prediction.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.970
The final answer is one point six

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.230
seven metres per second to the

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.980
right, rounded to two decimal

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.830
places.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.120
The carts approach with unequal

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.460
signed velocities.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.260
When they meet, they stick.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.130
Both then move right together, more

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.230
slowly than cart A moved initially.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.790
The total momentum remains five

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.180
kilogram metres per second to the

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:47.950
right.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.160
Their individual momenta have

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.060
changed.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.400
What stays the same in this sticking

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.260
collision?

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.260
Choose total momentum, each cart's

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.640
momentum, or total kinetic energy.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.070
Pause and give a reason using the

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.000
system and the external force.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.810
Total momentum stays constant under

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.940
the stated external-force condition.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.520
The carts exert equal and opposite

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.220
forces on one another, giving

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.940
opposite momentum changes.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.880
In this sticking collision, kinetic

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.370
energy decreases as energy is

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.070
transferred into deformation,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.910
internal energy and sound.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.960
Total energy is still conserved.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.920
Increase only cart B's mass to three

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:20.900
kilograms.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.310
Keep both initial velocities

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.260
unchanged.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.340
Predict the new final velocity, then

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.860
calculate it on paper.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.600
Choose zero point six zero to the

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.850
right, the original velocity, or

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.900
zero point six zero to the left.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.500
Pause before continuing.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.120
The new calculation gives a total

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.250
initial momentum of plus three and a

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.360
combined mass of five kilograms.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.040
The shared velocity is zero point

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.190
six zero metres per second right.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.620
Increasing this leftward-moving

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.780
cart's mass both reduces the total

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.770
rightward momentum and increases the

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.420
mass that must move together.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.790
Test your reasoning in the Collision

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:53.440
lab.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.700
Set the original masses and

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.400
velocities, and select the sticking

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.210
collision.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.720
Run and compare the total momentum

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.930
before and after.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.630
Then change only cart B's mass to

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:02.870
three kilograms.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.510
Explain the result before opening a

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.610
worked answer.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:06.800
Small differences from hand

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.430
calculations can come from displayed

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.280
rounding.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.690
Try this fresh question without

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.660
looking back.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.390
Cart A and cart B now have equal

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:14.210
masses.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.950
Sketch the directions, retain the

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.840
signs, choose your equation and

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.270
state the final velocity with its

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.550
unit and direction.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.820
Pause and complete your working

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.930
before checking.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.840
The final velocity is one point zero

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.750
zero metres per second right.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.460
If your answer differs, check the

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.570
negative velocity first, then check

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.060
that you used both masses after the

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:32.910
collision.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.880
Correct the faulty step, and retry a

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.600
fresh question in Check and review

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.420
later.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.060
Recall the method from memory:

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.630
sketch and sign, conserve the total,

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.140
then solve and interpret.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.470
Use the simulation to test

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:45.980
predictions and the handwritten

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.720
checkpoint to show your reasoning.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.170
A later independent attempt will

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.460
tell you more than simply watching

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.680
the solution again.
